    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d409">

                <pb facs="0514" n="426" xml:id="pg426"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Griscom to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Tokyo,
                                Japan</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-08-26"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 26,
                    1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith copy
                    of a letter from the minister for foreign affairs elated yesterday, with which
                    he sent me a statement of the position of the Japanese Government and of their
                    negotiations with China regarding the Russian warships <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Askold</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Grosovoi</hi> remaining at
                    Shanghai.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lloyd C. Griscom.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d409-a1.xml" xpointer="d409-a1"/>
